WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.899
. This is very, very interesting.

00:00:02.899 --> 00:00:09.860
Many Republicans have been demanding smaller
packages from Democrats, as we talked about

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:10.860
yesterday.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.959
Jen Psaki, regularly.

00:00:12.959 --> 00:00:17.650
Minded of the fact that all these different
Republicans say Biden's package is too big,

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:22.200
they need a smaller package, Mitt Romney is
doing something very interesting.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.830
Mitt Romney is a Republican senator.

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:31.610
He has a proposal to provide three thousand
dollars per child to millions of American

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:32.610
families.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:41.329
And this would be a form of bipartisan support
for Joe Biden's covid relief plan, which includes

00:00:41.329 --> 00:00:43.360
expanding child benefits.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.780
Now it's a slightly different framework.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:52.780
Romney would give forty two hundred dollars
per year per child up to age six.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:59.180
That goes down to three thousand dollars per
year per child for age six to 17.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:04.500
And how that would interact with some of these
other elements is in the details that that

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.299
we are still learning about.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:12.450
But what is very interesting about this is
that one of the reasons that Mitt Romney and

00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:17.979
maybe some other Republicans are interested
in this is that they think if you give these

00:01:17.979 --> 00:01:27.880
bigger payments to people, they will be less
likely to file the return.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:28.880
I'm sorry.

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.729
Let me go backwards.

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:37.200
Republicans believe that giving payments would
discourage parents from finding jobs.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.479
And this is their concern with what Mitt Romney
and also with what Joe Biden are proposing.

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:49.719
This is this very old trope that we hear from
the right, which is predicated on the idea

00:01:49.719 --> 00:01:54.920
that everybody's lazy and nobody has any drive
or motivation.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:58.700
And people just want to figure out how to
not work at all.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:02.270
Most people, you know, there's an evolutionary
thing to this.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:07.280
And when we read some very interesting articles
about, you know, people who feel unfulfilled

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.660
and all these different things, there are
practical reasons for that, people seeking

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.580
meaning and fulfillment.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:19.830
But there may also be an evolutionary reason,
which is when you were fulfilled, human advancement

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:21.230
potentially stopped.

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:26.240
When you were satisfied, you stopped trying
to improve your circumstances and those of

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:28.290
your children and their children and so on.

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:30.970
So there may even be an evolutionary basis
for this.

00:02:30.970 --> 00:02:34.130
But most people want to do something most
people want, meaning?

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:40.770
Yes, there are some people who, for a variety
of different reasons, want the easiest path

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:41.770
out.

00:02:41.770 --> 00:02:45.340
If I can just sit at home and not work and
collect money, that's fine.

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.120
Most people don't want that.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:54.010
Most people want one job that pays well so
that they can have some meaning coming from

00:02:54.010 --> 00:03:01.240
employment and also have the financial wherewithal
to be able to raise kids, put food on the

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:05.590
table for family, participate in life in other
ways.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:09.700
And this Republican idea that if you do this,
it always assumes the worst about people's

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:12.830
intentions and the worst about humanity.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.280
And that's really how these Republicans see
people.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:20.550
But I'm glad to see Mitt Romney proposing
proposing an alternative to this.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:26.990
Now, this is going to be the way that Romney's
idea would be integrated, is that Mitt Romney

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:32.890
wants it to be an amendment to the Democratic
budget resolution.

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:37.870
And it looks as though a budget resolution,
budget reconciliation is increasingly likely

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:41.450
to be the way that this covid relief bill
is going to be passed.

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:48.640
And as I've said before, the fact that Democrats
can pass this without any Republican involvement

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:53.010
to me signals the time for so-called negotiation
with Republicans is over.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:55.870
But I don't believe every Republican will
vote against it.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:04:00.959
I believe that there are Republicans that
either for personal political convictions

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:05.870
or because of their realization that covid
relief is popular with their constituents.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:11.040
Some Republicans are going to vote for this
and put up call them on their bluff.

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.040
Right.

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:16.010
See if they actually are all going to vote
against the one point nine dollars billion

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:17.010
package.

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:20.739
If that's what Democrat Democrats go forward
with, I don't believe that they will.

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:25.719
And in particular now with Mitt Romney jumping
in, which makes this listen, I always thought

00:04:25.719 --> 00:04:30.499
it was naive to think you're going to get
this big bipartisan covid relief bill when

00:04:30.499 --> 00:04:36.960
the party of Republicans is the party of obstruction,
but merely Mitt Romney saying, here's an idea

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.100
and then I'm in favor of it.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:42.409
It makes it technically bipartisan, even if
nobody else comes on board.

00:04:42.409 --> 00:04:44.930
So I think these are very, very interesting
developments.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:49.490
And to be very clear, I know there are people
who keep writing to me saying, Davey boy,

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:54.300
why aren't you calling out Biden for the fact
that he said 2000 and now it's fourteen hundred?

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.960
And why aren't you calling out Biden for the
fact that he said the checks would go out

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:57.960
right away and they haven't?

00:04:57.960 --> 00:04:58.960
I have called him out.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.809
I called him out in just about every segment
I've done, including on yesterday's show.

00:05:02.809 --> 00:05:07.129
Joe Biden has already not done what he promised,
which is he said it would be two thousand

00:05:07.129 --> 00:05:12.680
dollars not to not 14 to get to a total of
two thousand with the last stimulus, Joe Biden

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:13.680
said.

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.750
Two thousand dollar checks, now they're talking
about 4500, that's already a problem.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:22.150
Joe Biden also said if Democrats win the two
seats in Georgia, checks go out right away.

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.759
Well, it's already February.

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:28.909
I understand this takes a little bit of time,
but it's time to move forward.

00:05:28.909 --> 00:05:33.949
It's time to do it with budget reconciliation,
whether or not Republicans want to be involved.

00:05:33.949 --> 00:05:37.629
And I hope I mean, listen, if Mitt Romney
proposing even more money for children is

00:05:37.629 --> 00:05:41.879
the way to make it bipartisan and get more
Republicans to support it, great.

00:05:41.879 --> 00:05:45.169
If not, it's time for Democrats to get it
done by themselves.

00:05:45.169 --> 00:05:46.169
Let me know your thoughts.

00:05:46.169 --> 00:06:29.029
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman,
The David Pakman Show 

00:06:29.029 --> 00:07:34.339
at David Pakman dot com.

